1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=157041638 Find A Grave]: '''Ane Nekoline Gabrielsdatter "Lena" Bryne Helland'''. Birth: May 19, 1882 in Kathryn, Barnes County, North Dakota, USA. Death: Aug. 21,
2 CONC  1969 in Assiniboia, Assiniboia Census Division, Saskatchewan, Canada. Burial: Mossbank Cemetery, Mossbank, Assiniboia Census Division, Saskatchewan, Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary (Southern Saskatchewan Newspaper, August 1969):<br/>
2 CONT Funeral service for the late Mrs. '''Lena Helland''', 87 years, was held Sunday August 24 from Messiah Lutheran Church with Rev. F.X. Muttoo officiating and Ross Funeral Home in charge. Interment followed in the Mossbank Cemetery.
2 CONC  Mrs. Margaret Dean rendered a solo, "Beyond the Sunset".<br/>
2 CONT Mrs. Helland the former Lena Byrne, was born in Kathryn, North Dakota, May 19, 1882, and in 1901 married Christopher Helland. They came to Canada in 1910, and homesteaded in the Ardill district residing there until 1954 when Mr. H
2 CONC elland passed away. She then resided in Moose Jaw until 1964 when she moved to Assiniboia, and lived with her daughter, Mrs. Gust Anderson. She had been hospitalized several times within the past year, and was a resident of Ross P
2 CONC ayant Nursing Home at the time of her death. She passed away at the Assiniboia Hospital, Thursday, August 21st.<br/>
2 CONT Mrs. Helland had been very active in her time, being like a nurse and home doctor to her community, especially as a mid-wife. She was also active in the Aldenburg Ladies' Aid.<br/>
2 CONT Predeceased by her husband and two grandchildren, she is survived by three sons, and four daughters, Olaf of Mossbank, Lawrence of Rockford Bridge, Alberta, Alfred of Ardill, Alma (Mrs. Gust Anderson), Assiniboia, Gladys (Mrs. Vin
2 CONC ce Nelson), Regina, Alice (Mrs. Andrew Norbraten) Windsor, Ontario, Minnie (Mrs. Norman Beattie) of Petawawa, Ont., also surviving are fourteen grandchildren, thirty-seven great grandchildren and five sisters.<br/>
2 CONT In lieu of flowers, gifts were received for the organ memorial fund of Messiah Lutheran Church.
