1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * FT 1875: Datter ug Hjelper Faderen: ØT: OPPEGAARDEN øvre
2 CONT * Utvandret 1878 #79 [https://sites.google.com/site/totenemigrant/Toten-emigrant-1846/1876-1880 Link]<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT "K. MATHILDA THORSON
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Mrs. John (Mathilda) Thorson, 95, were held Friday from the First Lutheran Church in Litchville with Rev. Alan Schmidt officiating. She died November 19, 1963. Interment was in the Litchville Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Thorson has been in failing health in recent months due to old age. She was hospitalized at the time of her passing.
2 CONT
2 CONT Karen Mathilda Oppegaard was born June 5, 1868, to Hendrick and Ane Oppegaard in Totten, Norway. She came to the United States with her parents in 1879 and the family settled in Fillmore County, Minnesota. In 1881 the family moved
2 CONC  to North Dakota locating in Nelson Township in Barnes County.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was baptized in Norway into the Lutheran faith and was confirmed in Sheyenne Valley Lutheran Church north of Kathryn. She had attended school in Minnesota.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1891 she was united in marriage to John T. Thorson in Valley City, where they made their home until 1902 when they moved to Litchville. In 1907 they moved to their farm southeast of Litchville and continued to live there until 
2 CONC 1929, when Mr. Thorson passed away on December 18, 1929. Mrs. Thorson and son Carl continued to live on the farm until 1957 when they moved into Litchville to make their home. She left her Litchville home a few months back when he
2 CONC r health became worse.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Thorson leaves to mourn her passing: one son, Carl F. of Litchville; five daughters: Nettie (Mrs. Gabriel) Berntson of Litchville; Henrietta (Mrs. George Olson) of Seattle, Wash.; Lillian (Mrs. Samuel) Anderson of Eau Claire,
2 CONC  Wis.; Effie (Mrs. Richard Eilts) of Marion; and Lorraine (Mrs. Charles) McClaflin of Chicago, Ill. There are 14 grandchildren and 37 great-grandchildren. She was preceded in death by her parents, her husband and two sons. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Coming from a distance to attend the funeral were: Mr. and Mrs. Howard Willey, Glasgow, Mont.; Mrs. Stanley Wendt, Bismarck; Mrs. Richard Triepke, LaMoure; Mr. and Mrs. Jay Chapman, Mandan; Mr. and Mrs. Donald Sweintek, Berlin; N.
2 CONC R. Nelson, Fargo; Mr. and Mrs. Henry Holanson, Fargo; Mr. and Mrs. Arthur Monson, Valley City; Mr. and Mrs. Harland Berntson, Sanborn; Mrs. Laura Vagle, Valley City.
2 CONT
2 CONT Blessed be the memory of this pioneer mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral arrangements were by Oliver's Chapel."
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in The Litchville Bulletin, Litchville, ND, November 1963. Bio by: Myrna (Lindstrom) McGregor
