1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Klepp Gards- og ættesoga gjenom 400 år, 1519-1900, Vik, side 315, nr. 45.c
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Klepp Gards- og ættesoga gjenom 400 år, 1519-1900, Vik, side 315, nr. 45'''
2 CONT Jan Olson, son åt Ola Sveinson, Erga nr. 67, f. 4/10 1794, d. 18/7 1863,
2 CONT G. 24/3 1836 m. Elen Marie Rasmusd., Anda nr. 54c, f. 24/4 1814, d. 3/7 1873.
2 CONT Born:
2 CONT * a. Anna Kirstine, f. 7/6 1837, g. m. nr. 69.
2 CONT * b. Ola, f. 25/1 1841, nr. 68.
2 CONT * c. Ingeborg Kirstine, f. 23/12 1842, d. 13/12 1866.
2 CONT * d. Elen, f. 28/10 1849, g. m. Andreas Olson, Vagle 42, Høyland.
2 CONT * e. Johan, f. 4/11 1855, Nærbø, skomakar.
2 CONT Jan fekk bøgsel på 18 sp. 16/5 1834, men 1844 fekk Sivert Rasmusson skøyte på den eine halvparten 9 sp. og 1852 fekk Asbjørn Asbjørnson skøyte på dei andre 9 sp. Jan var seinare husmann.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Baptized January 1 1843: Ministerialbok Klepp 1842 - 1852, page 11 Godparents: Lisbeth Rasmusdatter Orrie, Ingeborg Rasmusdatter Anda,Helga Sivertsdatter Vig, Nils Rasmusen Anda, Tønnes Torkelsen ibid
2 CONT
2 CONT Confirmation October 4 1857: Ministerialbok Klepp 1853 - 1870, page 142, number 20
2 CONT
2 CONT Cencus Klepp 1865: Ingeborg Kristine is maid at the Pollestad farm.  (Den transkriberte folketellingen for 1865 på Arkivverket/Digitalarkivet kaller henne Jonsdatter).
2 CONT
2 CONT When she gives birth to her daughter Johanne October 30 1866, she lives at Vig, where she was born and raised. She was an unmarried mom; maybe she was fired from her job at Pollestad? The father of her child, Bjørn Larsen, was a l
2 CONC odger at the Pollestad farm. He was a teacher and churchsinger that later emigrated to America. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried December 20 1866: Ministerialbok Klepp 1853 - 1870. page 300, number 29
2 CONT Klepp sokneprestkontor, SAST/A-101803/001/3/30BA/L0005: Parish register (official) no. A 5, 1853-1870, p. 300
2 CONT Quick link: https://www.digitalarkivet.no/kb20051212040987
