1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Services were held last Wednesday at the Sinai Lutheran Church for Herman Thompson, 78, lifetime Sinai area resident who died at the Brookings County Hospital April 14, 1990.The Rev. Mark Svaren officiated. Music w
2 CONC as by the Sinai Mens Quartet and organist was Mrs. Arnold Hope. B urial was in West Sinai Cemetery. Johnson-Henry Funeral Home of Arlington and Lake Preston was in charge.Honorary pallbearers were Arland Raad, Lyle Erickson, Charl
2 CONC es Langum, Bernard Torgrude, Norman Nelson, Kenneth Nelson, Clifford Thompson and Albert Swenson.Pallbearers were Allen Husher, Marvin Hope, David Negstad, Mark Stime, Reuben Skordahl, and William Buck.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Thompson was born Oct. 9, 1911, near Sinai, son of Julius and Malena (Wallem) Thompson. He attended school in Sinai and married Lila Madsen of Arlington Dec. 26, 1935.The couple farmed near Sinai for several years. Herman drov
2 CONC e the Sinai School Bus and was custodian at the Sinai Lutheran Church for 32 years.In 1963 the couple moved into Sinai. He worked at South Dakota State University and at Pamida in Brookings before his retirement in 1984.He was an 
2 CONC active member of Sinai Lutheran Church and the Sinai Senior Citizen’s Group.
