2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/94434048/rachel-bergeson
2 CONT
2 CONT From a History of Hamilton and Clay counties, Nebraska / supervising editors George L. Burr, O.O. Buck ; compiled by Dale P. Stough, 1921
2 CONT
2 CONT Ole and Rachel (Runestad) Bergeson, both natives of Norway, whence they came to the new world, settling in LaSalle county, Illinois, in 1856. There Ole purchased a farm upon which he and his wife spent their remaining days. They h
2 CONC ad a family of six children: B. O.; Erasmus, living near Earlville, Illinois, Mrs. Malinda Thompson, whose husband is a retired farmer of Paxton, Illinois; John, a physician of Boston, Massachusetts, who is specializing on disease
2 CONC s of the eye, ear and nose; S. E., a banker and merchant of Bismarck, North Dakota; and Mrs. Mary Dahl, whose husband is a merchant of Paxton, Illinois. Having lost his first wife Ole married a second time and there were six child
2 CONC ren of that union of whom five survive: Anson, now a retired farmer living in Iowa; Julia, the wife of Thomas Sawyer, a capitalist of Humboldt, Iowa; Borem, a farmer and banker living at St. Cloud, Minnesota; Nelson, a farmer and 
2 CONC grain dealer and shipper located at Swea City, Iowa; and Eddie, who is engaged in farming at Swea City. Ole was a member of the Lutheran church and its teachings were a guiding force in his life. His political endorsement was give
2 CONC n to the republican party. In his business affairs he displayed thoroughness and capability and won success as the years passed on.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachel Rasmusdatter Runestad was born at Talje in Finnøy kommune.
2 CONT
2 CONT dau/o: Rasmus Johnsen and Malene Sevatsdatter Runestad
2 CONT
2 CONT Church book from Talje confirms(No. 10, right side):
2 CONT
2 CONT https://media.digitalarkivet.no/view/8814/35
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachel married Ole Bergesen Uhr on 1 Apr 1851
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://media.digitalarkivet.no/view/1588/121
2 CONT
