1 NAME Jakob Bergson /Bergson/ d.y
2 GIVN Jakob Bergson
2 SURN Bergson
2 NSFX d.y
2 _MARNM Langhus
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1677
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Norway
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1757
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Brukte Nordland fra 1716. Skruss-Eikeland fra 1721.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Gro Tollachsdatter on August 23 1716 in Høyland, Rogaland, Norway (Ministerialbok Høyland 1691 - 1732, Ekteviede 1711 - 1717)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Some sources, including here at Geni, claim that Berg Kristensen Langhus (Grøsareid) had another son named Jakob Bergsen Nordland/Skruss-Eikeland. '''Is there any evidence that Jakob Bergsen Nordland/Skruss-Eikeland was a son of B
2 CONC erg Kristensen Langhus (Grøsareid)?'''  "Høyland: gards- og ættesoga" states that he was, both in the section on [https://www.nb.no/items/d63bfb43198e89d1eb04c0cdcae2d40d?page=306 Nordland] and [https://www.nb.no/items/d63bfb43198
2 CONC e89d1eb04c0cdcae2d40d?page=366 Skruss-Eikeland]. Yet, neither his [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070619650673 engagement record dated 19-07-1716]; nor his [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070619650683 marriage record dated 2
2 CONC 3-08-1716] makes any reference to his origin. Furthermore, [https://www.nb.no/items/d63bfb43198e89d1eb04c0cdcae2d40d?page=306 "Høyland: gards- og ættesoga"] states that he was born 1677 and died 1757. Yet, the Jakob Eikeland that 
2 CONC died in 1757, before his [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070619660233 burial record dated 20-03-1757], is claimed to have been 68 years old at death, '''thus born about 1689, i.e. 14 years after the death of his supposed father
2 CONC , Berg Kristensen Langhus (Grøsareid)'''. Moreover, in three probates listing the children of Berg Kristensen Langhus (Grøsareid) there is only reference to one son named Jakob; namely: the probate after Berg Kristensen Langhus (G
2 CONC røsareid) [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/sk20081106650287 dated 24-08-1675]; the probate after the only known child of his son Ole Bergsen Langhus, namely Anna Olsdatter Hetlandsgrunn, [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/sk200811067300
2 CONC 86 dated 25-06-1767]; and the probate after his son Erik Bergsen Langhus (Øystad-Øvre) [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/sk20081106650312 dated 22-03-1676]. In the second of these probates it becomes clear that the Jakob listed there
2 CONC  is Jakob Bergsen Langhus (Askje) (based on the names of his children listed there).
2 CONT ----
