1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=160100396 Find A Grave]:<br/>
2 CONT Obituary (''Litchville Bulletin'', Litchville, North Dakota, November 2, 1988):<br/>
2 CONT '''Ervin Wenneson''', 73, formerly of Valley City, died in a Moorhead, MN nursing home Monday, October 24, 1988. The funeral was conducted October 28 at the North LaMoure Lutheran Church with Rev. Lee Herberg officiating. Burial w
2 CONC as in the church cemetery.<br/>
2 CONT He was born November 22, 1914, in the Litchville community, the son of John and Bessie Wenneson. He received his education in a rural school.<br/>
2 CONT Mr. Wenneson moved to Valley City in 1948 where he worked as a carpenter until retiring. He had been in a nursing home the past three years. He had never married.<br/>
2 CONT He is survived by two brothers, Morris and Harry of rural Litchville; five sisters, amy (Mrs. Carl) Grindahl, and Ella (Mrs. Walter) Grindahl, both of rural LItchville; Mertis Palmer of Casper, WY; Ruby Parks, Walnut Creek, CA; an
2 CONC d Gladys (Mrs. Vernon) Johnson, Kellogg, MN; and a number of nieces and nephews.<br/>
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his parents, two brothers and two sisters.<br/>
2 CONT Pallbearers were Neil and Douglas Doty, Bill Englehardt, Ray and Wayne Wenneson and Wayne Johnson.
2 CONT ------
2 CONT Variation of spelling: '''Erwin''' and '''Irvin'''.
