1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dåp: 24. Aug. 1845: Østre Toten prestekontor, Ministerialbok nr. 2, 1840-1847, s. 47: https://www.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070202630053
2 CONT
2 CONT Konfirmasjon: 14. oktober 1860 i Balke kirke, Østre Toten prestekontor, Ministerialbok nr. 4, 1857-1865, s. 182: https://www.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070202630675
2 CONT
2 CONT Viede: Østre Toten prestekontor, Ministerialbok nr. 5, 1866-1877, s. 244: https://www.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070202640398
2 CONT
2 CONT * FT 1865: Deres Datter ug: ØT: Oppegaard øvre, Sarenødegaard
2 CONT * FT 1875: hans Kone: ØT: OPPEGAARDEN øvre
2 CONT * Utvandret 1878 #78 [https://sites.google.com/site/totenemigrant/Toten-emigrant-1846/1876-1880 Link]<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Ved dåp, konfirmasjon og folketellingene i 1865 og 1875, benevnes hun bare "Anne". Først ved vielsen, 1868, står det: "Anne Kjerstine". I emigrasjonsprotokollen 1878, står det: "Anne Christine" På gravsteinen står det: "Anne Kerst
2 CONC ine"
2 CONT
2 CONT "Mrs. Henrik Oppegard died last Saturday at her home southwest of town at the age of 70 - the Psalmists allotted three score and ten. Mrs. Oppegard was born in Norway May 4, 1845, and has been in this country 40 years. Her husband
2 CONC  preceded her in death a year and a half ago. Six children are left to mourn a kindly, Christian mother,viz: Mrs. John Thorson, Mrs. Mads Larson, Haagen and Miss Gussie of Litchville, Mrs. Olga Nelson of Fargo and Mrs. Minnie Swan
2 CONC son of Valley City. The funeral was conducted from the home on the Schlindeldecker farm on Tuesday afternoon. Rev. Jothen officiated and Oscar Larson, L.M. Olson, J. N. Lekvold, R. Schindeldecker and I. Gjerding acted as pall bear
2 CONC ers. May she rest in peace." Bio by: Myrna (Lindstrom) McGregor
