2 CONT "Mrs. Minnie Swanson, nee Oppegaard, died at Duluth on Christmas day, December 25, 1918, from influenza. The body was shipped here on Monday and buried late Wednesday afternoon, by the side of her parents, Hendrick and Anna Oppega
2 CONC ard, with Rev. Froyen officiating.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deceased was born in Norway on November 3, 1877, and came with her parents to Barnes County in the spring of 1880. For many years she made her home in Valley City, but has been living at Duluth the past three years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Swanson is survived by a son, Oscar Swanson of Valley City; four sisters and a brother, namely: Mrs. John Thorson, Mrs. Mads Larson and Haagen Oppegaard of this place; Mrs. N. R. Nelson of Moorhead and Mrs. C. A. Simenson of 
2 CONC Lonira, Alberta."
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in The Litchville Bulletin, Litchville, ND December 1918.
