1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Harland Berntson, 92, rural Sanborn, ND died at Mercy Hospital in Valley City, ND on March 10, 2017, while surrounded by his family and under the care of CHI Hospice.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral service will be held at 2:00 PM, Thursday, March 16, 2017 at Grace Free Lutheran Church, Valley City. Burial will be in the Zion Lutheran Cemetery later in the spring.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harland Lloyd Berntson, the son of Gabriel and Nettie (Thorson) Berntson, was born December 7, 1924 on the family farm. He attended a country school near Hastings, ND and graduated from Hastings High School. Harland attended the N
2 CONC orth Dakota State School of Science in Wahpeton, ND where he learned welding. After receiving his education, Harland worked for Strinden’s in Litchville, ND for a time.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harland enlisted in the National Guard October 2, 1950 where he served as a rifleman at Camp Rucker, AL. He was very proud of his Company G 164th Infantry Division and enjoyed many local reunions. He was a member of the Valley Cit
2 CONC y AmVets Post #3. After his discharge, he returned to the family farm where he worked with his father and uncle, John Berntson.
2 CONT
2 CONT On September 30, 1959, he married Arlene Olson. They lived in Lisbon, ND where he worked for the Chrysler Dealership. They moved to a farm near Sanborn in 1961. Harland spent many hours tinkering in his shop, perhaps to get a litt
2 CONC le quiet time away from his wife and five children. He was able to fix almost anything, but was partial to Ford Pickups and International tractors. He did buy a Dodge once, which caused quite a stir. He also had a life-long love o
2 CONC f horses and was very knowledgeable on blood lines and training. As a young man he racedquarter horses, and has many trophies to show for it. A person would have to ask to see his trophies as Harland was not one to brag. He enjoye
2 CONC d taking his family to many trail rides and horse shows around the area. He liked nothing better than to be out with the new colts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harland loved spending time with his grandchildren, and was known to tease them as all Berntson’s do. He loved holding babies and was a special grandpa to all of his grandchildren. Harland was a member of Zion Free Lutheran Church
2 CONC  of Green Township of Barnes County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harland is survived by his wife Arlene; five children, Marie (Jim) Eggert, Brian Berntson, Carol McAllister, Rhonda (Shannon) Day, and Steve Berntson; six grandchildren; two great-grandchildren; one sister, Elinor Chapman; three n
2 CONC ephews; three nieces.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harland was preceded in death by his parents, two brothers, Clifford and Merton and his uncle John."
2 CONT
2 CONT Adapted from Lerud-Schuldt-Mathias Funeral Home obituary
