1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Arla May (Eilts) Triepke, 89, of LaMoure, ND, died Friday, November 6, 2015 in the Oakes Community Hospital, Oakes, ND. Arla had been a resident of St. Rose Care Center for 10 months.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arla was born July 22, 1926 on her grandma's farm near Litchville, ND to Richard and Effie (Thorson) Eilts where she lived until age 7. Her dad's occupation as a maintainer operator took her to Verona, Adrian, Edgeley, and Marion.
2 CONC  Arla has four younger sisters whom she was very close to.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arla sewed her first garment at age 12. She turned a skirt into a pair of shorts on a treadle machine without a pattern. This was the beginning of her lifelong career as a talented seamstress.
2 CONT
2 CONT On April 7, 1944, she married Richard Henry Triepke. They had one son, Larry and one daughter, Vicki. Her husband Richard died on April 7, 1965.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arla started sewing for others about 1950. Besides alterations, she did many custom wedding garments, including wedding dresses, bridesmaid and flower girl dresses. She did many tux alterations, with some being the day of the wedd
2 CONC ing. She would also get calls for rush hem jobs on trousers and dresses that would be needed within the hour. Arla also sewed many prom dresses and did some drapery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arla was a member of Zoar Lutheran Church, American Legion Auxiliary and Past Presidents Parley. She was active in the Zoar Lutheran Church quilting group. Her hobbies included quilting, hardanger, crocheting, embroidery, making p
2 CONC orcelain dolls, rubber stamping greeting cards, making homemade buns and goodies and scrapbooking. She was the family photographer and made many cherished memory photo books. She made handmade Christmas ornaments every year for fa
2 CONC mily members. Her craft talent has been handed down through many generations. She had a love for cats, especially her black and white Persian Oreo who she had for many years. She loved her family and enjoyed being with them. She w
2 CONC ill be missed immensely by her family and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arla is survived by her son Larry (Eileen) Triepke and her daughter Vicki (James) Robideau; four sisters, Mavis Worsham, Marlis Willey, Darlene Swiontek and Diane (Orville) Otterson; five grandchildren and ten great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her husband, Richard, her parents, Richard and Effie Eilts, her brothers-in-law, Kenneth Worsham, Howard (Mack) Willey and Donald Swiontek.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral Service: Thursday, November 12, 2015 at 10:30 at Zoar Lutheran Church, LaMoure, ND.
2 CONT
2 CONT Interment: Rosehill Cemetery, LaMoure, ND."
2 CONT
2 CONT Adapted from Dahlstrom Funeral Home obituary
