1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Dale McClaflin, 76, of Rockford passed away Tuesday, May 10, 2011, in Arizona. Born Jan. 1, 1935, in Valley City, N.D., the son of Charles and Lorraine (Thorsen) McClaflin. Dale married Sylvia Powell on June 15, 1
2 CONC 963, in Chicago.
2 CONT He was a sales manager for United Laboratories. Dale served in the Army. He was a member of Holy Family Catholic Church. Dale was an inspiration to his family who always came first in his life. He had a great sense of humor and co
2 CONC uld always put a smile on your face. He was passionate about the game of golf and became an avid pickleball player while wintering in Arizona. He enjoyed great friends, good food, and a fine glass of wine. The spirit of Dale will 
2 CONC always live on in the hearts of those who knew and loved him.
2 CONT Survived by his best friend and loving wife of more than 47 years, Sylvia; son, Mike (Heidi) McClaflin of Phoenix; daughters, Deb Clark of Byron and Michelle (Jim) McGinnis of Spokane, Wash.; grandchildren, Grant and Dominic Arps,
2 CONC  Michael and Charlie McClaflin, Jake Clark, Jess and Chance McGinnis; and sister, Charlotte Kurzeja of Wonder Lake. Predeceased by his parents.
2 CONT Memorial funeral Mass at 10:30 a.m. Saturday, May 21, at Holy Family Catholic Church, 4401 Highcrest Road., with visitation from 9 to 10:15 a.m.; the Rev. Andrew Mulcahey and Deacon Michael Cristoforo will officiate. In lieu of fl
2 CONC owers, memorials may be made to the Leukemia and Lymphoma Society Donor Services, P.O. Box 4072, Pittsfield, MA 01202, www.lls.org. Fitzgerald Funeral Home and Crematory, Mulford Chapel, assisted the family."
2 CONT
2 CONT Published by Rockford Register Star from May 19 to May 20, 2011.
